# enclave-pqc-primitives standards

- Keep changes minimal and focused. No unrelated refactors.
- One module per primitive family: `kem/`, `sign/`, `symmetric/`, `hash/`, `kdf/`, `encoding/`.
- Product SDKs must not import `@noble/*` directly — only this package.
- Algorithm IDs come from `registry/ENCLAVE_PQ_SUITE_v1.json`, not hardcoded strings.
- Validate inputs at public API boundaries (key lengths, empty buffers, malformed encodings).
- Tests live in `tests/`, not under `src/`.
- Barrel `index.ts` files own public exports; implementation files stay private to their folder.
- No god files. Keep files under ~120 lines when practical.
